Many English learners already know enough vocabulary, grammar, and prepared
answers to get through a simple exchange. The difficulty starts once the
prepared answers run out — a pattern sometimes called 哑巴英语 (literally,
"mute English"): able to answer, but not able to continue.

EnglishOS is exploring that different problem: not how to learn more English,
but how to use the English you already have to keep a conversation going —
and eventually get to know another person.

The aim is not simply longer conversations. It is helping people move from
speaking to sustaining, to deepening, to connecting, to building
relationships.

EnglishOS is an emerging implementation of the broader ConversationOS idea —
the same framework behind MandarinOS, applied to English conversations. It is
under active development now, not a finished product.
